 ### Rhombus Signed Distance Function
-*   **Definition**: Computes the signed distance function for a rhombus with semi-axes $s$ and height $h$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Steps**:
-    1.  Calculate $f$ using the dot product of $s$ and $s - 2p_{xz}$, clamped to $[-1, 1]$ [S1, unofficial].
-    2.  Calculate $q_x$ as the length of the vector from the rhombus edge minus the radius, multiplied by the sign [S1, unofficial].
-    3.  Return the signed distance using the min/max/length formula for box-like shapes [S1, unofficial].
